name 'designing-reliable-apps-postassessment-q13_2025'

question 'A teammate suggests handling all three outcomes of a recipe fetch — loading, empty result, and API unreachable — with a single message: "Something happened." Why is this a poor design decision?'

wrong 'Because a single message is harder to code and increases the amount of JavaScript the app needs to run'
wrong 'Because all three outcomes are technically errors and the browser requires separate handlers for each'
wrong 'Because users prefer longer, more detailed messages and a single short message frustrates them'
right 'Because each state communicates a different situation — treating them identically leaves users without the context they need to take action'

allow_multiple_attempts true

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
